#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Kaligiran {#background}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) is a variant of SKQD that replaces the need to choose an ansatz from which to sample bitstrings with an ensemble of time-evolution circuits constructed directly from the target Hamiltonian. This is achieved by subsampling smaller time-evolution operators from the Hamiltonian based on its coefficients, which is known as the qDRIFT Trotterization method.\n"
msgstr "Ang [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) ay isang variant ng SKQD na sa halip na pumili ng ansatz na pagkukunan ng sample ng bitstrings, gumagamit ito ng ensemble ng time-evolution circuits na direktang binuo mula sa target Hamiltonian. Nakakamit ito sa pamamagitan ng pag-subsample ng mas maliliit na time-evolution operators mula sa Hamiltonian batay sa mga coefficient nito, na kilala bilang ang qDRIFT Trotterization method.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial makes use of [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) to create the more natural fermionic circuits for the [qDRIFT](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.070503) algorithm, followed by the use of fermionic layout and synthesis passes before plugging the circuits into the traditional Qiskit pipeline for hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) para gumawa ng mas natural na fermionic circuits para sa algorithm na [qDRIFT](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.070503), na sinusundan ng paggamit ng fermionic layout at synthesis passes bago i-plug ang mga circuit sa tradisyunal na Qiskit pipeline para sa hardware execution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the Hamiltonian be of the form:\n"
msgstr "Hayaang ang Hamiltonian ay sa anyong:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i h_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i h_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where, without loss of generality, we require $c_i > 0$ and that the largest eigenvalue of $h_i$ be equal, in absolute value, to $1$. Any signed or complex prefactor is absorbed into $h_i$, so the coefficients $c_i$ are strictly positive weights while the $h_i$ carry the direction of each term. Here $N$ is the number of terms (or, after grouping, the number of groups) in the Hamiltonian; it is a property of the Hamiltonian and is distinct from the number of operators sampled into a single circuit, written $n$ below.\n"
msgstr "kung saan, nang hindi nawawalan ng generality, kinakailangan natin na $c_i > 0$ at ang pinakamalaking eigenvalue ng $h_i$ ay pantay, sa absolute value, sa $1$. Anumang may-sign o complex na prefactor ay isinasama (ina-absorb) sa $h_i$, kaya ang mga coefficient na $c_i$ ay mahigpit na positive weights habang ang $h_i$ ay may dalang direksyon ng bawat term. Dito, ang $N$ ay ang bilang ng terms (o, pagkatapos ng grouping, ang bilang ng groups) sa Hamiltonian; ito ay property ng Hamiltonian at naiiba sa bilang ng operators na na-sample sa iisang circuit, na isinusulat bilang $n$ sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qDRIFT algorithm then realizes, for the target time $t$, some operator $V_k$, where $k$ goes from $1 \\cdots K$ and signifies the $k_{th}$ SqDRIFT circuit, defined as:\n"
msgstr "Para sa target time na $t$, ipinapatupad ng qDRIFT algorithm ang isang operator na $V_k$, kung saan ang $k$ ay mula $1 \\cdots K$ at kumakatawan sa $k_{th}$ SqDRIFT circuit, na tinutukoy bilang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_k = \\prod_{j=1}^{n} e^{-i h_{k_j} \\lambda t / n }\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_k = \\prod_{j=1}^{n} e^{-i h_{k_j} \\lambda t / n }\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here $n$ is the number of sampled operators per circuit and $K$ is the number of circuits in the ensemble. The product runs over the $n$ draws, not over all $N$ Hamiltonian terms, and because the terms are drawn with replacement, the same $h_i$ can appear more than once in a single $V_k$.\n"
msgstr "Dito ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng sampled operators bawat circuit at ang $K$ ay ang bilang ng circuits sa ensemble. Ang produkto ay tumatakbo sa $n$ na pagkuha, hindi sa lahat ng $N$ Hamiltonian terms, at dahil kinukuha ang mga term nang may replacement, maaaring lumabas nang higit sa isang beses ang parehong $h_i$ sa iisang $V_k$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantity:\n"
msgstr "Ang dami:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is the $L_1$ norm of the coefficients, so each of the $n$ steps evolves for the same duration $\\lambda t / n$ regardless of which term was drawn. The uniformity of the step angle is the characteristic feature of qDRIFT: a coefficient influences the result through *how often* its term is drawn, not through how far that term is rotated. The indices are sampled from the distribution:\n"
msgstr "ay ang $L_1$ norm ng mga coefficient, kaya bawat isa sa $n$ na hakbang ay nag-e-evolve sa parehong tagal na $\\lambda t / n$ anuman ang term na nakuha. Ang pagkakapareho ng step angle ang katangiang tampok ng qDRIFT: ang isang coefficient ay nakaaapekto sa resulta sa pamamagitan ng *gaano kadalas* na nakukuha ang term nito, hindi sa pamamagitan ng kung gaano kalayo umiikot ang term na iyon. Ang mga index ay kinukuha mula sa distribution:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P[k_i] = \\frac{c_i}{\\lambda}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P[k_i] = \\frac{c_i}{\\lambda}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so the series $(k_1, \\ldots, k_n)$ is a random sequence of term indices drawn from this distribution. Since the $c_i$ are positive and sum to $\\lambda$, this is a normalized probability distribution, and the expectation of the resulting channel over the random draws approximates evolution under $H$, with an error that decreases as $n$ grows. Note that the approximation error depends on $\\lambda$ rather than on the number of terms $N$.\n"
msgstr "kaya ang series na $(k_1, \\ldots, k_n)$ ay isang random sequence ng term indices na kinuha mula sa distribution na ito. Dahil positive ang mga $c_i$ at ang kabuuan nila ay $\\lambda$, isa itong normalized probability distribution, at ang expectation ng resultang channel sa mga random draws ay tinatantya ang evolution sa ilalim ng $H$, na may error na bumababa habang lumalaki ang $n$. Tandaan na ang approximation error ay nakadepende sa $\\lambda$ sa halip na sa bilang ng terms na $N$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(The SqDRIFT paper writes the number of terms as $\\mathcal{N}$ and the sequence length as $N$; we use $N$ and $n$ here to keep the two clearly distinct.)\n"
msgstr "(Isinusulat ng SqDRIFT paper ang bilang ng terms bilang $\\mathcal{N}$ at ang haba ng sequence bilang $N$; ginagamit natin ang $N$ at $n$ dito para panatilihing malinaw ang pagkakaiba ng dalawa.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to generate an ensemble of such randomized circuits. After we have created these circuits, similar to how we create a Krylov subspace for different operators, we sample bitstrings from multiple such operators with different time parameters. This ensures a higher overlap between the ground state vectors and sampled bitstrings.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng tutorial na ito kung paano bumuo ng ensemble ng ganitong mga randomized circuits. Matapos nating gawin ang mga circuit na ito, katulad ng paggawa natin ng Krylov subspace para sa iba't ibang operators, kumukuha tayo ng sample ng bitstrings mula sa maraming ganitong operators na may iba't ibang time parameters. Sinisiguro nito ang mas mataas na overlap sa pagitan ng ground state vectors at ng sampled bitstrings.\n"

